  "raw_text": "Stripping ANSI escape sequences from terminal recordings was established as a necessary preprocessing step before session transcripts can serve as input to a text pipeline such as vivify. The approach considered was a Python `re.sub` pattern to remove ANSI sequences, with `ansistrip` from bsdutils named as the standard tool. This positions ANSI stripping as a recurring infrastructure concern whenever raw terminal output is treated as a document.",
